,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":38.074151311,"data":"- chance that at least one of our 8 seeds learns (6 here + 2 on the workstation): unknown. If each seed had the paper's cross-backbone rate (e5-\u003egtr: 3 of 15 seeds), about 1 - 0.8^8 = 0.83. The paper also reports gte-\u003egtr failing without per-pair tuning, so zero is a real possibility and would itself be a result\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":38.074168353,"data":"- native-1M (positive control): should learn: it is the authors' own pair and pipeline. If it does not, the budget per run is too short and a failure of our pair is inconclusive\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":38.074173017,"data":"- native-50k vs native-1M: if 1M learns and 50k does not, too little data is the problem (Aman's hypothesis)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":38.074176796,"data":"- dpr_matched vs ours: if dpr_matched learns and ours does not, more / matched victim-side data helps\n"}
